#31100
@@yWestern Approach Road@@N~
@@yA broad track of compacted desert clay runs east from the oasis basin, its surface pressed firm by generations of loaded sleds and pack animals.
@@bLow cairns painted with @@ysun-gold@@b survey marks still flank the road at regular intervals, their faded pigment catching the morning light.
@@yEach cairn bears a distance glyph and a bearing line cut into its eastern face — the beginning of the Reach's accountancy of space, where every mile was once a taxable quantity.
@@bThe air here carries the mineral dryness of the deep desert behind you, but something changes faintly at the eastern horizon: a sharper mineral edge that smells of salt crust rather than open sand.
@@yThis is the threshold where oasis jurisdiction gives way to the long legal corridor of the Reach, and the cairn marks begin to matter.@@N
