@@yDust-Choked Milestone@@N~
@@yAn eroded Keeper survey stone stands at the road's edge, its carved graduation marks worn to shallow ghosts by centuries of abrasive wind.
@@bThe milestone's eastern face still bears a partial inscription: a bearing line and a tidal glyph that once encoded distance to the coast in terms of expected flooding hours — the Keepers' characteristically precise and impractical measurement.
@@yGrit has settled into every carved groove, so that the inscription is legible only in the slanted light of early morning, and then only to someone who already knows what they are looking at.@@N
