@@yCaravan Muster Ground@@N~
@@yA broad packed-earth clearing serves as the first gathering point for convoys assembling to cross the Reach — wagon poles propped against each other, draft animals staked in loose rows, cargo bales stacked under reed-mat shade canopies.
@@bThe ground is worn in concentric loops where animals have circled their tie-stakes for so many seasons that their paths have become semi-permanent features of the landscape.
@@yTo the north a road leads toward the Northern Oasis approaches, and the ambient hum of commerce — quarreling assessors, braying animals, and the creak of harness fittings — fills the warm air.@@N
