#31105
@@yStaging Yard@@N~
@@yThe Staging Yard is the operational heart of the western Reach — a wide expanse of hard-packed ground where caravan marshaling, transit-seal checking, guide-hiring, and faction negotiation happen simultaneously and often loudly.
@@bWarden patrol bands occupy the northern quadrant, their ironwood staves planted in the ground during status conferences that look more like territorial claims than coordination meetings.
@@yGlasswalk Guides congregate at the southern edge, identifiable by the distinctive chitin-soled sandals worn looped to their pack frames — the famous glasswalk shoes, worn only when the glass terrain begins.
@@bRed Sand Counting House agents move through the crowds with brass scales and wax-sealed ledger pouches, offering services that never quite sound predatory until the repayment schedule is discussed.
@@yFive road exits radiate from the yard: back west toward the oasis basin, north toward the warden barracks, south toward the guide camp, and two tracks departing east toward the Mirror Flats — one swift, one heavy.@@N
