@@yAt the alley's eastern end, the Red Sand Counting House facade presents its most reassuring face: brass-mounted scales visible through the front window, a clerk's quill perpetually moving across a manifest, and the smell of good quality lamp oil suggesting the ledgers burn long into the night.@@N
