@@yRed Sand Counting House@@N~
@@yThe Counting House interior is aggressively respectable: polished brass fittings on the weighing scales, neat stacks of sealed ledger pouches, a conversion table showing Reach water-debt rates alongside current maritime assessment equivalents — precisely the document that traps inland cargo owners who don't know what shore conversion actually costs.
@@bA Red Sand counting clerk works at the central desk with the focused efficiency of someone who has performed the same calculation hundreds of times and enjoys the moment when the client realizes what the final number means.
@@yA stairway at the back leads to an upper office where the Counting House's station manager handles the larger accounts — the caravan leagues, the distressed cargo purchases, and the debt instruments that will be presented at Mafdet's docks.@@N
