@@yHeavy Road Gate to the Flats@@N~
@@yThe last cairn of the western Reach stands here like a sentry — taller than the others, its capstone carved with a tide glyph and a bearing marker that points due east toward the Mafdet coast, the Reach's only directional guarantee that the Flats crossing goes somewhere specific.
@@bThe Flats begin immediately east of this cairn, the salt crust extending to the horizon in a hard, white, blindingly reflective surface that makes the air above it shimmer even at a distance.
@@yA worn inscription on the cairn's western face reads in Survey-Administrative voice: bearing shoreward-east confirmed, distance two days loaded, assessment required at first major station, glasswind advisory check at guide waystation before Belt entry.@@N
