@@yExtra descriptions mounted on the eastern wall present sample inscription text in the Survey-Administrative, Legal-Conversion, and Guide-Oral voices — the three textual traditions that overlap in the Reach's physical infrastructure, now preserved in paper copies because the stones themselves are being dismantled by scavengers faster than they can be transcribed.
@@bA small display case holds a genuine cairn tablet fragment: sandstone bearing four intact Littoral Branch glyphs — a tidal measurement notation, a cargo-draft specification, a bearing line, and a witness-seal acknowledgment — representing the Keepers' attempt to bring their entire legal system to bear on the problem of loading a ship.@@N
