@@yBlinding Heart — Southern End@@N~
@@yThe southern end of the diversion connects back to the north loop through a narrow section where the two paths approach each other to within a few body-lengths — close enough that a confused traveler trying to use sound as a navigation reference will hear footsteps from both directions and cannot determine which are their own echo.
@@bThis section is where guides plant the most markers per unit distance — a dense cluster of basalt pegs and cord guides that provides navigation for clients who have lost all other reference, a kind of tactile map through the most genuinely disorienting section of the crossing.
@@yThe maze exits are accessible from both the northern and eastern paths; this section is purely for demonstration and for those who have wandered in from an unexpected direction.@@N
