@@yGlasswind Belt Entry@@N~
@@yThe entry into the Glasswind Belt from the Swift Line route is a specific narrow passage that guides know and maintain because the glass terrain on either side of it is actively hostile — the passage is wide enough for a single file of travelers with appropriate footwear, and narrow enough that departing from it in either direction puts you in glass terrain immediately.
@@bThe wind through the passage carries glass dust in perceptible quantity — a fine abrasive that accumulates on exposed skin surfaces over time and is removed with difficulty because the particles are too small to shake off but too large to be safely rubbed.
@@yThe sound of the Belt is immediately different from the Flats: a constant low abrasive whisper from the glass surfaces interacting with each other and with the wind, punctuated by the occasional crack of a shard under pressure or the hollow ring of a glass surface over a worm void.@@N
