@@ySwift Line Belt Section@@N~
@@yThe Swift Line's path through the northern edge of the Glasswind Belt is the most maintained section of the Belt — guides clear glass debris from the route regularly, and the chisel-notched stone waymarkers are replaced when broken by glass impacts rather than left to accumulate weather damage.
@@bThe belt here is in the milky glass zone — the older, stable glass that gives firmer footing and less cutting risk than the amber and violet zones further south and east — making this the least dangerous section of the Belt even as it is more demanding than anything on the Flats.
@@yThe route continues east toward the Glasswind Eastern Exit and the approach to the cairn district, the final structured section of the Reach before the territory opens into the contested zone around Measure's Rest.@@N
