@@yA zone of elevated salt deposition creates a low ridge across the Heavy Road here, the accumulated product of lateral seep from a mineral-rich substrate section that reacts with the overlying salt crust to produce secondary crystal growth.
@@bCaravan hands have been chipping away at the ridge for many generations — both as a practical road-clearing exercise and as a source of usable salt crystal that supplements the standard brine-preserved rations — creating a low channel that is technically improved road but is actually just the ridge carved down to acceptable grade by accumulated individual effort.
@@yThe channel through the ridge is the narrowest point on the Heavy Road, requiring wider sleds to proceed with care and narrowing loads to single-file foot traffic when the route is busy.@@N
