@@yFortified Waystation@@N~
@@yThe Fortified Waystation is the most intact major structure in the Mirror Flats South crossing — an assessment hall that survived the Fracture Era's violence through the combination of defensible construction, a relatively neutral position in the competing jurisdiction maps, and the practical consensus that a rest stop on the Flats is worth preserving even if no one agrees who owns it.
@@bThe interior is large enough to shelter a significant convoy: the main hall with its intact wind-baffle canopy system, the side cistern room to the north whose mineral stratification serves as an unintentional geological record of the crossing's water-supply history, and the assessment platform to the south where the weighing scales once operated.
@@yThe walls display competing authority marks from four different factions — Reach Wardens, Red Sand Accounts, an unnamed Fracture-Era caravan league whose insignia is no longer recognizable, and the Glasswalk Guide camp's condition-board — the four marks occupying different walls and maintaining a fragile visual truce.
@@bThe waystation serves as the Heavy Road's navigation reference point: from here, the Sealed Route junction lies east, the Second Assessment Station south, the Third Assessment Station and the Cairn Line approach further east still, and the route markers calibrate their distances to and from this hub.
@@yA stone bench runs the full length of the eastern wall, worn smooth by the many caravan crews who have rested against it waiting for assessment, transit seal verification, or the simple passage of time in a place that is reliably solid after days of crossing uncertain terrain.@@N
