@@ySaltglass Threshold@@N~
@@yThe first glass begins here — not the dramatic crystalline sweep travelers imagine, but a tentative scattering of milky shards among the salt, as if the desert is testing whether you will turn back before committing to the transformation.
@@bThe milky coloration is reassuring. Glasswalk Guide oral tradition distinguishes three colors with distinct significance: milky glass is pre-catastrophe formation, stable and firm underfoot; amber glass marks thermal fault proximity and unstable crust; violet glass marks eclipse-rite residue zones, where the Synod Whisper Cells find theological significance and where the ground occasionally hums at night.
@@yA waymarker post driven into the crust at the threshold bears Guide-scored notches that form the first line of a route song — an orientation mnemonic that a trained Guide can sing to navigate the entire Belt from memory, the oral infrastructure that replaced the written waymarks that the Ninth Meridian's heat consumed.@@N
