@@yGlasswalk Guide Waystation@@N~
@@yThe Waystation is the only uncontested neutral ground in the entire Saltglass Reach — a compact structure built from salvaged milky glass blocks mortared with a desert-resin compound, roofed with layered sailcloth panels that diffuse the overhead light into a quality that does not produce glare off the glass floor.
@@bThe Glasswalk Guides established the Waystation through a trilateral agreement with the Reach Wardens and the Red Sand Outriders — both factions benefit from having a reliable crossing service, and both understand that harming Guide neutrality would end the service that makes the Glasswind Belt navigable for their own supply lines. The Synod Whisper Cells were not party to the agreement but have tacitly respected it, since they also depend on Guide knowledge to move through the Belt undetected.
@@yThe interior smells of the Guide-specific resin compound used to clean and reseal glass-scorpion wounds — a sharp mineral-botanical combination that becomes, for frequent crossers, the smell of safety. A guide roster board near the entrance shows which routes are currently mapped as safe, updated daily in the route-song notation that serves as the Guild's internal written system.
@@bThree exits lead east, north, and south into the Belt from here, representing the three route options a crossing party must choose between: the northern thermal ridge route, the central main crossing, and the southern approach through scorpion and shrine territory. Each has advantages depending on current conditions.
@@yServices available here include guide hire, route song lessons, emergency supply resupply at surcharge rates, first aid for glass-abrasion and scorpion encounters, and — at the discretion of the senior Guide on duty — access to the current worm migration mapping that determines which glass sections are currently collapse-risk.@@N
