@@yWorm Warren Eastern Exit@@N~
@@yThe eastern edge of the worm warren system surfaces here — the collapse that created the accessible portion of the warren at its west end is mirrored by a smaller breach at the east end, where the worm channel simply ran out of glass belt and entered the mixed terrain of the Belt's eastern margin.
@@bThe breach here is older than the western entry, long since stabilized and partially obscured by glass particle accumulation. The warren system the worm traversed to reach this exit ran the full east-west extent of this section of the Belt — a transit distance that implies a worm significantly larger than any the Glasswalk Guides have documented in their behavioral records.
@@yThrough the breach, the terrain changes character — the dense glass of the Belt proper gives way to a mixed landscape where glass shards thin out among sand and gravel, the first indication that the Eastern Glass Shelf and the cairn district beyond are within reach.@@N
