#31305
@@yStation Two: Toll Hall@@N~
@@yThe second station is better preserved than the first — its Toll Hall structure survives to partial roof height on two walls, creating a sheltered space that the current competing claimants have found useful as a base of operations.
@@bThe competition is visible in the toll signs: three different parties have posted competing toll schedules on the surviving walls, each in a different script and claiming a different authority. The Reach Wardens' notice invokes the original Littoral Branch charter. A Red Sand Outrider notice invokes their purchased claim to specific station parcels. A third notice, in the flowing script of a party that has not identified itself, quotes a legal precedent from the Fracture Era that may predate the Wardens' charter entirely.
@@yThe physical signs have been modified by each party in turn — scratched out, re-inscribed, damaged in ways consistent with deliberate removal attempts, patched with additional text. The layered modification record represents the legal dispute made visible: three parties each convinced of their authority, unable to resolve the claim, defaulting to posting competing notices and hoping the other parties will eventually concede.@@N
