#31314
@@yScavenger Sorting Depot@@N~
@@yThe depot is an organized operation — the Scavengers working this district have divided the stripped materials by type and quality, creating sorting piles of bronze components, lead plugs, assessment platform hardware, and the various stone and ceramic materials that turn out to have secondary market value despite the scavengers' initial focus on metal.
@@bSome of the sorted materials appear to be significant archaeological finds — tablet fragments mixed in with the bronze hardware, possibly recovered incidentally during the metal extraction operations. The Scavengers appear not to have recognized the tablets as distinct from ordinary stone debris, since the fragments are sorted into the stone pile rather than the market-valuable items.
@@yA Scavenger supervisor is present, conducting an inventory with notched tally sticks — a counting system that appears to track the number of items by category rather than weight or value, suggesting the market transactions are negotiated by item count rather than assay weight.@@N
