@@yScavenger Market@@N~
@@yThe informal market in stripped cairn materials occupies a sheltered corner of the Crossroads compound where three wall sections create a natural enclosure. The market is well-established enough to have regular traders, a tacitly accepted rate schedule for common materials, and a dispute resolution process that functions without formal authority.
@@bThe materials available include bronze fitting components at various stages of processing (raw stripped, cleaned, and in a few cases shaped into secondary products), lead plugs useful for metalworking and construction, carved stone pieces with inscriptions intact (which attract a collector market separate from the raw stone trade), and the occasional intact small object — a writing instrument, a pocket-scale weight, a document seal — that fetches a premium.
@@yThe Reach Wardens permit the market by not prohibiting it — a pragmatic arrangement that keeps the Scavengers concentrated in a visible location and provides the Wardens with intelligence about what materials are being extracted from the ruins. Several of the regular traders appear to be Warden informants; the Scavengers appear aware of this and conduct their most sensitive business elsewhere.@@N
