@@yFaction Boundary Zone@@N~
@@yThe boundary between the Scavenger-active zone and the Warden-controlled zone is not a wall or a gate but a perceptible shift in the quality of the ground and air — the Warden-maintained section literally looks different, maintained surfaces contrasting with the scavenger-disturbed rubble.
@@bBoth factions have chosen to mark the boundary in their own terms: the Scavengers have left territorial markers at the boundary's western edge (scratched into stone, their identifying notation), and the Wardens have posted a formal notice at the boundary's eastern edge (a legal declaration that the eastern section is under Warden administrative jurisdiction and subject to their search and seizure authority).
