@@yLandward Tidewright Cell@@N~
@@yThe Landward Tidewrights are an archaic scholarly order that predates both the current Warden structure and the Fracture Era — their tradition traces to the original Littoral Branch scribes who developed the Measure Script and the Shore Conversion tables. They maintain their presence in the cairn district specifically to access the surviving tablet records before further decay or scavenger activity removes them.
@@bThe Cell consists of three scholars currently in residence, conducting the painstaking work of full Measure Script transcription — copying every legible tablet inscription into their own notation system to preserve the content even if the tablets are subsequently lost or destroyed. The work is proceeding in the order of conservation urgency: most damaged tablets first, regardless of their content significance.
@@yThe scribes are cooperative with scholars and researchers who can demonstrate competence in Measure Script or related notation systems, and deeply suspicious of everyone else. They have their own legal position on the tablets in Measure's Rest: that the original Tidewright succession maintains scholarly custody rights that supersede Warden administrative control, a claim that the Wardens dispute but have chosen not to force to a confrontation given the Tidewrights' connections.@@N
