@@yMeasure's Rest: Outer Court@@N~
@@yThe Outer Court of Measure's Rest is the Reach Warden fortress's public face — the enclosed exterior courtyard between the gatehouse and the main structure's entrance, where petitioners wait, scholars conduct preliminary negotiations for archive access, and Warden patrols brief and debrief.
@@bThe court preserves the best sense of the original Crossroads compound's design intent: high stone walls with surviving parapet courses, an interior surface maintained clear of debris, and the triple-route stone mosaic at the court's center still largely intact — a decorative element that doubled as a legal display, showing the three route certification seals interlocked in the compound assessment symbol.
@@yThe mosaic is the most visited object in the Reach for scholars — the triple certification seal's full design survives here and nowhere else, the other examples having been stripped or defaced. Three trade delegations currently occupy three corners of the courtyard, each waiting for Warden authorization to access the archive for different purposes, each pointedly not acknowledging the others.
@@bWarden Sentinel Korvast Dune commands the Outer Court — a compact, methodical officer whose filing system for access petitions is more elaborate than the military defensive protocols for the fortress. Access to Measure's Rest's archive is, in her assessment, both more valuable and more contested than the physical structure, and she treats the petition review process accordingly.
@@yThe fortress gate leading north into the main complex requires Korvast's direct authorization — she does not delegate this to junior wardens, citing too many incidents of archive access being granted to parties who had not been properly vetted. The wait for authorization can be hours or days depending on the complexity of the petitioner's stated purpose.@@N
