#31345
@@yCairn Capstone Observatory@@N~
@@yThe Cairn Capstone Observatory is the most complete surviving example of the Littoral Branch's astronomical survey infrastructure — the measurement station that established the distance and bearing reference points for the entire Reach's navigation system, translating celestial observations into the terrestrial distance notation recorded on every cairn marker.
@@bThe circular platform is intact: twelve socket holes around the circumference, each oriented to a specific celestial reference point at the correct measurement season, the sockets deep enough to hold shadow-rods of standardized length in precise vertical alignment. The measurement geometry that the platform encodes represents a sophisticated astronomical and mathematical understanding that the surviving tablet records only partially explain.
@@yThe capstone collection around the platform's base — toppled markers brought here from across the district, their celestial reference notations accumulated into a comparative set — is the research prize that the Kowloon scholars most want access to. The platform sits at the junction of the outer cairn ring's eastern passage and the southern approach corridor.@@N
