@@bThe containers in the yard ahead were sealed for transit — the sealing compounds were not permanent containment materials but transit-grade sealants designed to last from origin to the Tidemouth conversion process. They have outlasted their design life by centuries, and whatever the sealant was protecting against is gradually escaping as the compound degrades.
@@yThe ominous quality of the approach is amplified by its visual character — the path narrows, the wall remnants close in, and the light quality changes as the path passes between surviving wall sections that reduce the sky to a stripe above.@@N
