@@ySealed Container Yard@@N~
@@yThe Container Yard holds thirty-seven containers that have been here since the Sealed Route's abandonment — stone chests with lead-sealed lids, bronze cylinders with crimped closures, and several ceramic amphora sealed with a hardened compound that has partially cracked with age.
@@bThe container manifest, posted on a surviving wooden board, lists the contents of each numbered container in the Hazard Reclassification notation. A scholar fluent in that notation can determine that the containers hold: eleven relic consignments from the Southern Pyramid network, seven from the Fractured Shore provenance system, twelve from unnamed originators (which the manifest codes as "legacy consignment — pre-Fracture"), and seven that the manifest lists as "Class Three: Undetermined Origin."
@@yThe Class Three containers are the ones with the most degraded seals — the containers whose contents required the most intensive hazard protocols, and whose sealants were perhaps most aggressively formulated and therefore most chemically reactive over time.@@N
