@@bThe Cells' theological framework treats the quarantine zone as a space where the ordinary rules of containment between the physical and spiritual are weaker than elsewhere — the accumulated hazard classification protocols, the physical sealing of objects whose nature was not fully understood, and the ongoing off-gassing from the aged container yard all contribute to an ambient quality that their theology interprets as spiritual presence made physical.
@@yThe ritual room's inscriptions cover every available surface — the Eclipsed Tongues theological text here is the most complete surviving version of the Vitrification Covenant theology, presented in the formal large-scale script that the Cells use for their most significant ritual texts, the verses interleaving with each other in a complex layout that requires the full circuit of the room to read in sequence.@@N
