@@ySealedRoute — Tidemouth Approach Transition@@N~
@@yThe terrain here begins to shift away from the Sealed Route's desert character toward the mixed desert-coastal environment of the Tidemouth Approach — the soil composition changes, the air carries more moisture, and the first maritime debris is visible: fragments of tar-soaked rope and sailcloth scraps blown inland from the coastal zone.
@@bThe transition marks the Sealed Route's geographic limit: the quarantine designation ends at the point where the Tidemouth Approach's maritime jurisdiction begins, the two legal systems meeting at a boundary that was never formally demarcated because the Sealed Route's suspension prevented the boundary negotiation from occurring.
@@yThe absence of a formal boundary between the quarantine designation and the maritime jurisdiction has created a legal gray zone that the current factions have found useful — the uncertain status of this transition section means that none of the standard authority frameworks applies cleanly, making it attractive for activities that none of the factions want to conduct under direct authority scrutiny.@@N
