@@bThe burrowing pattern that creates the ledges reflects the crab population's slope-management behavior: they burrow horizontally into the slope face rather than vertically, creating a series of horizontal galleries that, combined with the root systems of the saltmarsh plants at each ledge level, stabilize the otherwise mobile dune material.
