@@yAnchor Stone Field@@N~
@@yThe Anchor Stone Field is the first concrete evidence that the coast is genuinely close — large basalt anchors from Mafdet's maritime operations deposited here over generations, too heavy to return to the harbor and not worth salvaging further inland, forming an irregular field of maritime artifacts in the coastal approach terrain.
