@@yResin dumps and sailcloth scraps appear alongside the anchors — the detritus of ship-maintenance operations conducted here rather than at the harbor itself, when the Tidemouth Approach's outer zone served as the preparation area for inbound ships and the offloading zone for outbound cargoes that the harbor's formal infrastructure could not accommodate.@@N
