@@bThe tidal range data inscribed on the marker represents the Keeper period's most intensive coastal survey effort — the systematic measurement of tidal variation across the Tidemouth zone that established the baseline data for the Shore Conversion system's maritime calculation tables. Without these measurements, the conversion system could not have operated.
