@@bThe surviving base section retains the lower portion of the inscriptions that covered the original obelisk — the base of the tidal calibration text, the beginning of the conversion calculation tables, and the foundation of the astronomical orientation markings that allowed the obelisk to function as both a tidal measurement station and a celestial survey point.
