#31424
@@yCoastal Marsh Path@@N~
@@yThe coastal marsh path follows the edge of the saltmarsh vegetation rather than crossing through it — a route that keeps travelers on firm ground while the marsh extends to the south, the vegetation dense enough that off-path movement through it would be slow and wet.
@@bThe marsh path is one of the more pleasant sections of the Tidemouth Approach — the vegetation provides wind shelter, the firm path edge makes footing reliable, and the marsh itself is home to a variety of coastal birds that create the ambient sound background of calls, wing sounds, and territorial displays that characterizes active marsh ecology.
@@yThe path shows heavy use — the Carter route passes here, the Warden patrol circuit passes here, and the general coastal traffic uses it as the standard approach in this section. The multiple use patterns have created a broad, well-worn surface that is easy to follow even in reduced visibility.@@N
