@@yResin Dump Clearing@@N~
@@yThe Resin Dump Clearing is a wide, flat area where Mafdet Harbor's ship maintenance operations deposited hull-caulking waste over several generations — a maritime industrial site that has been abandoned long enough to become an archaeological feature rather than an active waste zone.
@@bThe accumulated resin deposits cover the ground in a series of poured layers that have hardened into a surface with different properties than the surrounding salt clay — the resin composite is firmer, less permeable to tidal water, and supports different plant colonization than adjacent terrain. Small organisms that find the resin surface beneficial have established populations here that do not appear elsewhere in the approach zone.
@@yScattered through the deposit are ship-maintenance artifacts: caulking mallets, rope scraps, ceramic vessels that held resin supplies, and in two places intact sections of wooden planking that were discarded as too deteriorated for further use and have since been partially preserved by the resin compounds that soaked into them.@@N
