@@yDual Jurisdiction Zone@@N~
@@yThe Dual Jurisdiction Zone is where the competing legal frameworks of the Reach Warden administration and the Harbor Warden maritime authority are both explicitly present and equally unenforceable against each other — a small area of coastal approach terrain that has become the physical manifestation of the larger jurisdictional question.
@@bBoth Warden forces have posted their full authority documentation here — the legal texts that establish their respective claims in the clearest and most complete form each can produce. The postings face each other across a gap of perhaps ten paces, the gap itself being the zone of maximum uncertainty where neither posting is clearly more authoritative than the other.
@@yThe practical effect is that the Dual Jurisdiction Zone is one of the most legally permissive areas in the coastal approach — not because no law applies, but because two sets of law apply simultaneously in ways that create gaps and ambiguities that sophisticated actors exploit. The Sand-Sea Carters' Guild has been the most systematic exploiter of these gaps, structuring their documentation to be simultaneously compliant with both systems while maximizing the operational flexibility that the gap zones provide.@@N
