@@bThe fog thins at this boundary due to the terrain change — the harder coastal ground of the Strand reflects heat differently than the marsh, creating a thermal boundary that partially suppresses the fog formation. Coastal travelers know the Strand begins when the fog lightens and the smell of the harbor district's maritime industry becomes detectable in the air.
@@yThe boundary also marks the transition from the Reach's administrative jurisdiction (even the contested version) to the undisputed Harbor Warden territory that covers the entire Mafdet Strand approach. The jurisdiction clarity here is a relief to travelers who have navigated the approach's contested zone.@@N
