#31445
@@yMafdet Strand Approach@@N~
@@yThe Mafdet Strand Approach is where the Saltglass Reach's journey terminates and Mafdet Harbor's world begins — the point where the Reach's administrative complexity gives way to the harbor district's commercial clarity, and where the Shore Conversion's legal architecture becomes the lived reality of maritime trade rather than ruined inscription.
@@bThe Strand itself extends eastward along the coast — a strip of firmer, developed ground that leads to Mafdet Harbor's landward gates. The Harbor Wardens control this approach entirely; the Reach's contested jurisdiction ends definitively at the Strand's western edge, and from here to the harbor, the Shore Conversion system's conversions that the entire Reach's infrastructure was designed to produce are actually conducted.
@@yLooking west from the Strand Approach, the Saltglass Reach is visible in its full extent — the coastal approach zones, the distant glint of the Glasswind Belt's amber glass on the horizon on a clear day, and in the far distance the salt-white expanse of the Mirror Flats that form the Reach's western terminus. The whole administrative and geographic system is visible in a single panoramic view.
@@bThe Harbor Wardens have their own characterization of the Reach, visible in the carved inscription at the Strand Approach's entrance: "here begins the shore, where inland law accepts the sea's terms." The inscription is recent enough to have been carved after the current jurisdictional dispute began, and its confident tone reflects the Harbor Wardens' assessment of who holds the stronger legal position.
@@yThe Strand Approach is the last room before the Shoreward Threshold district's processional route begins — the formal final approach to the Shoreward Seal and its adjacent Assessment Halls, where the actual legal conversion of inland transit certification to maritime documentation takes place. The Strand is where travelers can see where they are going; the Threshold is where they get there.@@N
