@@yShoreward Processional Hub@@N~
@@yThe Processional Hub is the central junction of the Shoreward complex — the point where the main processional axis from the Processional Court meets the cross-axis that connects the Heavy Road Assessment Hall to the north with the main conversion facilities to the east.
@@bThe Hub's layout makes the three-route system's functional organization visible: north leads to the Heavy Road's more elaborate assessment facilities, south leads back toward the Sealed Route's specialized conversion, and east continues toward the core conversion facilities where all three routes' cargo ultimately underwent the Shore Conversion's final procedures.
@@yA formal inscription at the Hub's center — a basalt marker with four-face notation — records the three-route jurisdiction in the compound assessment formula: all certified cargo, regardless of approach route, enters equal legal status from this point eastward, the distinctions that the Hall assessments managed dissolving in the compound authority of the Shoreward Compact.@@N
