@@yAssessors' Practice Area@@N~
@@yThe practice area where Assessors in training conducted their conversion exercises using simulated cargo scenarios rather than live consignments — a teaching facility where mistakes did not have legal consequences, allowing the training process to develop competency before exposing clerks to actual conversion work.
@@bThe practice scenarios were standardized in tablet form — a library of training cases covering the full range of cargo types, conversion challenges, and special circumstances that working Assessors might encounter. The tablet library is partially intact and represents the most comprehensive surviving educational resource on the Shore Conversion process.
@@yThe practice scenarios include a category of extreme cases — conversions that the training system used to test Assessors at the limits of their competency, involving cargo categories that had no established precedent or that presented genuinely unresolvable conflicts between the inland and maritime legal frameworks. The existence of these extreme case tablets implies that such conversions occasionally occurred in actual practice.@@N
