#31462
@@yShoreward Table Hall@@N~
@@yThe Shoreward Table Hall is named for its primary feature — the conversion ratio charts carved directly into the hall walls, the most comprehensive and authoritative surviving record of the Shore Conversion system's mathematical tables.
@@bThe tables cover every cargo category recognized by the system: weight-to-volume conversions for bulk goods, value-to-risk translations for insured cargo, the Hazard Reclassification conversion tables for regulated materials, and the special case tables for cargo types that required multiple conversion steps. The inscriptions cover every available surface and were updated periodically, as evidenced by the overlaying of later corrections over earlier values in the most frequently revised table sections.
@@yReading the tables — for a scholar competent in both Measure Script and the maritime notation system — reveals the economic logic of the Shore Conversion: the conversion ratios implicitly encode the relative value of inland and maritime legal frameworks, and tracing how those ratios changed over time reveals the economic history of the Reach's trade balance with the maritime world.@@N
