@@yDual Attestation Chamber@@N~
@@yThe Dual Attestation Chamber is where both the inland seal and the maritime seal were applied to completed conversion documentation — the physical act of dual sealing that made a conversion document legally valid in both jurisdictions simultaneously.
@@bThe dual sealing process required two separate officials: the Shoreward Assessor applying the inland seal (derived from their training and certification under the Littoral Branch framework) and the Harbor Representative applying the maritime seal (derived from the Harbor Charter's authority). Both officials had to be present and willing for any conversion to be completed.
