@@yUndercroft Descent@@N~
@@yThe Undercroft Descent is a stairway cut directly into the bedrock beneath the Shoreward complex — not the construction materials of the above-ground facilities but the pre-existing rock substrate, the excavation preceding the complex's construction by an unknown period.
@@bThe stairway construction is different from everything above — a simpler, more massive style that suggests older techniques and possibly a different builder culture than the Shoreward complex's primary construction period. The Compact's reference to a foundational mechanism predating the Keeper period appears credible in light of the construction style evidence.
@@yA locked stone door at the base of the descent prevents casual entry to the Undercroft — the lock mechanism is the same complex double-bitted style used for the Sealed Relic Vault in the Sealed Route, suggesting a common key authority or a common locksmith tradition. The door shows evidence of failed opening attempts: scratch marks around the keyhole from instruments that were not the correct key.@@N
