@@bThe control elements include adjustment levers for each of the engine's disc assemblies, a reference chart inscribed in the chamber wall that appears to show the correspondence between above-ground jurisdictional conditions and the correct disc settings, and a log of previous settings inscribed in a continuous record that spans more adjustment events than the above-ground complex's operational period.
@@yThe log pre-dates the Keeper period — the earliest entries use a notation system that the Kowloon scholars tentatively identify as proto-Measure Script, suggesting continuous operation of the jurisdictional mechanism across multiple administrative frameworks, each new system inheriting and adapting the mechanism rather than creating its own.@@N
