@@yLair of the Shoreward Revenant@@N~
@@yThe lair of the Shoreward Revenant occupies what was originally the mechanism's primary witness station — the position from which the pre-Keeper operators observed the mechanism's state and recorded its outputs. What now occupies the space is something that was once an operator, transformed by centuries of exposure to the mechanism's unresolved jurisdictional conflict into something that is neither living nor dead by the standard definitions of either framework.
@@bThe Shoreward Revenant is the embodied contradiction of the conversion system — an entity that exists in both the inland and maritime jurisdictional frameworks simultaneously, unable to fully belong to either, continuously experiencing the legal conflict that the conversion system was designed to resolve. Its aggression toward visitors reflects a territorial preservation of the only space where its contradictory existence is tolerated by the mechanism's ambient field.
@@yThe chamber itself bears the marks of the Revenant's extended tenure: surfaces worn smooth by repeated contact, specific positions that the Revenant apparently occupies regularly, and a residue of the conversion system's chemical signatures accumulated from centuries of the Revenant's physical processing of the mechanism's conflict field.@@N
