a drywell attendant~
A weather-worn attendant tends the sealed well access with quiet pride in their maintenance work.
~
The drywell attendant's role in the staging ground is unglamorous but essential — monitoring water access, maintaining the filtration system, recording draw amounts against the supply ledger, and enforcing draw limits during the dry season. Their familiarity with the Reach's water situation is encyclopedic, accumulated through years of watching caravans arrive desperate and calculating exactly how much they could carry versus how much they needed. The attendant has opinions about both the Wardens' transit taxation and the Red Sand Accounts' water-debt instruments, and will share both if asked.
~
