cairn tablet reader~
a cairn tablet reader~
A scholarly figure squints at a stone tablet fragment through thick glass lenses, muttering notation comparisons.
~
The tablet reader's portable magnifying glass — itself a remarkable piece of Glasswalk craftwork — is fixed on a fragment of cairn-station tablet bearing what appears to be a third notation system alongside the familiar Measure Script and Littoral Branch. Three reference volumes lie open around them, each bookmarked at relevant passage. The reader is from the scholarly annex attached to the Reach Warden administrative complex, ostensibly to assist with cairn identification but in practice pursuing a long-running personal investigation into the pre-Keeper survey notation that predates both the Wardens and the Tidewright Schism.
~
