#31110
caravan drover~
a caravan drover~
A drover tends the animal pen with the patient ease of someone comfortable with long silences.
~
The drover manages the pack animals in the staging ground's holding pen, an occupation that requires more expertise than it appears — desert-crossing animals have specific dietary, hydration, and hoof-care requirements that differ from inland stock, and a drover who doesn't know the difference loses animals on the Flats. This one has clearly made the crossing many times, judging by the ease with which they handle the animals and the practiced efficiency of the pre-departure inspection they are currently conducting.
~
