The staging yard rat is bigger than its inland cousins, fed on the rich scraps of transit-hub commerce — spilled ration bricks, dropped trail food, the occasional piece of cargo that bounced off a sled. Its confidence suggests it has won enough confrontations with other scavengers to believe it owns this particular patch of ground.
~
