salt cricket swarm~
a salt cricket swarm~
A dense, chirring mass of salt-white insects surges forward with disorienting speed.
~
The salt cricket swarm moves as a coordinated mass rather than as individuals — thousands of pale insects whose salt-bleached carapaces catch the light in rippling flashes. The sound is extraordinary, a physical presence of clicks and scrapes that can disorient even experienced Flats travelers. Individual crickets are trivial; the swarm is something else entirely, capable of overwhelming larger prey through sheer numbers and the disorientation caused by the sound and motion.
~
