#31114
cairn kite~
a cairn kite~
A broad-winged raptor rides the thermal currents above the salt flats, fixing its target with pale predatory eyes.
~
The cairn kite takes its name from the habit of nesting in the upper reaches of the old cairn markers, using the height for both shelter and survey. From above, the pale expanse of the Mirror Flats is a hunting ground — the kite can spot the movement of prey from extraordinary distances and drops in a controlled stoop that makes full use of the speed built up in the descent. Its talons are disproportionately long relative to its body, adapted for snatching prey from the salt crust surface.
~
