cairn kite alpha~
a cairn kite alpha~
The alpha kite is distinctly larger than its hunting companions, its pale plumage marked with salt-crystal deposits that flash in the light.
~
The alpha cairn kite commands the thermal column that the smaller kites hunt below — it takes priority on the best thermals and the choicest hunting territories. Salt deposits on the leading edges of its wings suggest it has roosted at a particularly mineral-rich cairn station, and the thickness of the deposits indicates this alpha is old and has held its territory for a long time. Its attack pattern is more varied than a younger kite's, incorporating feints and misdirection that reflect accumulated hunting experience.
~
