#31116
salt crust lurker~
a salt crust lurker~
Something beneath the salt crust moves with the rippling, purposeful motion of an ambush predator aligned toward prey.
~
The salt crust lurker exploits the hollow spaces beneath the Mirror Flats' crystalline surface, lying in wait with a stillness broken only by the occasional blind probe of sensory tendrils above the crust. When prey's vibration pattern matches its prey profile, it erupts upward through the crust in a strike designed for speed rather than finesse. Its secretions are toxic — a secondary defense mechanism against prey that survives the initial strike and attempts to fight back. The venom causes progressive muscle weakness that the lurker uses to make a second strike at a disadvantaged target.
~
