#31117
brine serpent~
a brine serpent~
A thick-bodied serpent with scales like faceted salt crystals moves with slow, deliberate confidence.
~
The brine serpent has adapted to the mineral seeps that dot the Mirror Flats, absorbing so much concentrated salt that its scales have taken on a crystalline texture that serves as both camouflage and armor. Its venom is processed through the same mineral concentration mechanism — a highly specialized toxin that disrupts fluid regulation in prey rather than attacking the nervous system, producing a slow but very reliable incapacitation. The serpent is patient in its hunting; it can lie motionless beside a seep for hours.
~
