swift line warden patrol~
a swift line warden patrol~
A compact warden patrol moves in a loose formation along the Swift Line route, checking cairn markers as they pass.
~
The Swift Line patrol moves with the efficient rhythm of a unit that has made this circuit many times — each cairn marker receives a quick structural inspection and notation in the patrol log, each transit seal impression in the approach zone is checked against the current day's valid-authorization list. The patrol's demeanor is professional and neutral, quite distinct from the degraded toll-thieves that haunt the less-supervised sections of the route. These wardens still believe in what the Reach Warden commission was founded to do.
~
