#31120
salt-blinded drifter~
a salt-blinded drifter~
A wanderer whose eyes have been permanently damaged by salt-flat reflection stumbles forward with desperate aggression.
~
The drifter was a traveler once, attempting the Mirror Flats crossing without adequate eye protection. The reflected light from the salt surface — concentrated and sustained over hours of crossing — has damaged their vision beyond recovery, leaving a pale film over both eyes and a sensitivity to light that manifests as pain and rage whenever any bright surface catches their attention. They attack anything that moves near them, driven by the confusion of permanent half-blindness in an environment of relentless reflected glare.
~
