waystation cistern keeper~
a waystation cistern keeper~
The cistern keeper sits at the well access with the particular stillness of someone who manages the only water for a long distance in any direction.
~
The Waystation cistern keeper is simultaneously a public servant and a power broker — the Reach crossing is possible only because of the waystation water supply, and whoever controls that supply has leverage that transcends any jurisdictional claim. The keeper tracks draw volume, monitors for contamination, and enforces the rationing limits that keep the cistern viable through the dry season. They also carry years of accumulated knowledge about the crossing conditions, the fauna patterns, and the route alternatives that the official transit maps don't show.
~
