convoy graveyard scavenger~
a convoy graveyard scavenger~
A scavenger picks methodically through the wrecked convoy remains, chipping bronze fittings free with expert efficiency.
~
The convoy graveyard scavengers have established a productive circuit through the wreck field, each salvager working a specific section of the ruins to prevent territorial overlap. This one's tools — chisels, pry bars, oiled wrapping cloth — are specialized for stripping bronze fittings from abandoned infrastructure while leaving the stone components that aren't worth carrying. The Reach salvage law is genuinely ambiguous about whether decomposing convoy remains constitute abandoned property, a fact the scavengers use as justification and the Wardens use as grounds for challenge.
~
