salt flat viper~
a salt flat viper~
A pale, narrow-bodied viper moves with the liquid grace of a creature perfectly adapted to crossing salt-crust surfaces.
~
The salt flat viper has evolved a locomotion pattern that minimizes contact with the reflective surface — side-winding in a pattern that keeps most of its body airborne at any point in the movement, reducing both heat absorption and the sensory disruption of the salt vibration. Its venom is highly concentrated, a desert adaptation that produces maximum effect from minimum delivery. It strikes low and fast, targeting the ankles of prey moving across the flat.
~
