The brine pool predator is specifically adapted to the hyper-saline water sources scattered through the southern Flats — it absorbs the heavy brine through its skin, using the salt concentration as both camouflage and as a chemical weapon, coating prey that comes to drink with a contact irritant that triggers flight responses. The predator then pursues at a speed that consistently surprises travelers who have assessed it as an aquatic creature limited to its pool.
~
