an assessment station ghost~
The ghost of a toll clerk still works at an invisible desk, stamping documents that no longer exist with seals that bear no weight.
~
The assessment station ghost is a manifestation of bureaucratic fixation outlasting its physical context — the clerk who inhabited this role was so thoroughly defined by the transit assessment process that their death did not interrupt the work. The ghost goes through the motions of document processing in a space where the desk, the papers, and the certification stamps have all long since crumbled to dust. When disturbed, it turns the same procedural attention to the source of the interruption, processing the intruder as a regulatory violation requiring correction.
~
