glass scorpion~
a glass scorpion~
A scorpion whose carapace has fused with the local glass deposits moves with predatory deliberateness through the belt.
~
The glass scorpion's carapace has been gradually replaced by fused silicate material absorbed from the Glasswind Belt's substrate, resulting in a creature that is simultaneously armored and partially translucent — the glass panels catch and refract light in ways that make accurate size estimation difficult. Its venom delivery system is augmented by the same mineral integration; the stinger is partly glass, partly chitin, and injects a compound that works differently from standard arthropod toxins.
~
