glass scorpion matriarch~
a glass scorpion matriarch~
The matriarch scorpion is considerably larger than the others, its glass-fused carapace spanning the full breadth of a desert road's wheel rut.
~
The glass scorpion matriarch commands a section of the Glasswind Belt's subsurface network, using chemical signals to direct the movement of younger scorpions through territories it has mapped over decades of hunting. Its glass integration is more complete than the younger scorpions — more surface area replaced by silicate, the translucency more pronounced, the refraction effects more disorienting. The stinger carries a venom concentration several times that of the standard glass scorpion, and the matriarch has learned to use the terrain's glass-refraction properties as cover during approach.
~
