glassworm burrower~
a glassworm burrower~
The ground shudders and splits as a segmented form erupts from the subsurface, trailing glass and sand.
~
The glassworm burrower is a subsurface apex predator of the Glasswind Belt, moving through a network of tunnels it has carved through the fused glass substrate. Its surface-breaking attacks are timed to prey's vibration pattern — the burrower monitors ground vibration from below, selects its moment, then erupts in a strike that uses the momentum of the emergence to amplify the impact of the attack. Its segmented body is sheathed in glass-integrated chitin that makes the creature naturally resistant to cutting weapons.
~
