glassworm tunnel sentinel~
a glassworm tunnel sentinel~
A massive glassworm coils defensively at the tunnel mouth, its acid-slicked maw tracking prey with patient hunger.
~
The tunnel sentinel is an elder glassworm that has claimed a key tunnel network junction, guarding access to the deeper burrowing zone through a combination of territorial aggression and the acid spray that it can project from glands developed in mature specimens. The acid is a weaponized version of the digestive secretion glassworms use to soften glass substrate for burrowing — concentrated, corrective, and effective at ranges that keep the glassworm inside the tunnel while its spray reaches prey at the entrance. The sentinel has maintained this position long enough that the tunnel walls show acid scoring that speaks to many encounters with the same result.
~
