#31135
glasswalk guide pathfinder~
a glasswalk guide pathfinder~
A focused guide stands at the waystation entrance, tapping the glass surface methodically with a chitin-soled staff before each step.
~
The pathfinder represents the Glasswalk lineage at its functional core — the reading of glass type and surface stability that makes traversal of the Belt possible without specialist equipment. Their staff's chitin tip produces a specific sound when tapped against glass that varies with thickness, composition, and the hollow-space risk beneath, and the pathfinder interprets this feedback with the automatic facility of someone who grew up learning the difference. They are available for hire and strictly neutral in Reach political matters, which they will mention unprompted to anyone who seems likely to assume otherwise.
~
