a synod lookout~
A wiry figure crouches behind a glass outcropping, scanning the approaches with obsessive vigilance.
~
The Synod lookout's position behind the glass formation is not random — the refraction properties of this particular outcropping create a perceptual distortion that makes the lookout difficult to spot from most approach angles while providing a clear view of the primary route. This is a feature of the Belt that the Synod has mapped carefully, identifying observation points that the Guides' route songs don't mention. The lookout carries signal material for alerting deeper Synod positions and is the first defense layer of the Whisper Cell network in this section.
~
