The glassworm burrower queen is the apex predator of the Glasswind Belt's subsurface system — the oldest, largest, and most dangerous glassworm in the territory, a creature around which the entire tunnel network has been organized over decades of her queen-directed expansion. Her glass integration is total along the forward segments; the chitin has been entirely replaced by fused silicate material, making her nearly impervious to conventional weapons along her leading surfaces. The acid glands that tunnel-sentinel glassworms use defensively have, in the queen, become primary weapons — she generates and projects acid at volumes and concentrations that dissolve glass substrate for burrowing but strip flesh with efficient brutality. The ground shudders noticeably with each of her movements through the tunnel system below.
~
