The tidal pool lurker is a specialist ambush predator that exploits the visual complexity of the tidal pool margin — the mix of brine, mineral deposits, algae, and shell fragments that characterizes the pool edge provides coverage for a creature that has adapted its coloration to match the combination precisely. It monitors the pool margin for the vibration pattern of drinking prey, then lunges in a strike that combines speed, a toxic secretion that it delivers through contact, and an attempt to drag prey into the pool where its aquatic advantage is total.
~
