brackish channel eel~
a brackish channel eel~
A sinuous form longer than a person is tall moves through the channel water with the boneless grace of a specialist aquatic predator.
~
The brackish channel eel has adapted to the Tidemouth's mixed-salinity water sources — it can operate in both the full-salinity tidal surge zones and the reduced-salinity brackish channels with equal effectiveness, making it a threat across the full width of the approach zone's waterways. It attacks from below the surface, using the brackish water's reduced visibility to approach within striking range before the prey has identified the threat. Its grip once established is extremely difficult to break; the eel uses the channel's current to assist in submerging prey.
~
