The tidemouth raider occupies the jurisdictional gap between the Reach Warden authority, which weakens as it approaches the coast, and the Harbor Warden authority, which has not yet formally extended to this transition zone. In that gap, with no consistent enforcement presence, the raider has established a toll-taking operation that is distinguished from the corrupted Warden toll-thieves primarily by the honesty of its nature — the raider does not pretend to be a legitimate authority, simply demands payment and makes the alternative clear. Their knowledge of the coastal terrain, including escape routes and ambush positions, is comprehensive.
~
