jurisdiction specter~
a jurisdiction specter~
A ghost that appears to be composed of overlapping map layers manifests, each layer contradicting the others in its territorial claim.
~
The jurisdiction specter is a unique manifestation specific to the Tidemouth's boundary zone — a haunting that represents not a single dead person but the accumulated energy of the Reach's unresolved jurisdictional contradiction, given ghostly form by the intensity of the competing claims at the point where they meet. It does not speak in any single faction's voice but in all of them simultaneously, producing an overlapping cacophony of transit authority mandates, maritime salvage law citations, Harbor Charter provisions, and Keeper survey inheritance arguments that is disorienting and eventually hostile. The hostility is not personal; it is the hostility of unresolvable contradiction.
~
