A weathered teamster supervises the transfer of sled cargo to maritime containers with the unhurried authority of Guild seniority.
~
The Guild teamster's seniority is visible in the quality of their equipment — better-maintained tools, a more comprehensive cargo manifest system, and the deference that younger crew members show as they approach with questions. The teamster's job is the most critical handoff in the Reach's economic function: the moment when inland transit cargo officially becomes maritime cargo, with all the jurisdictional and insurance implications that shift entails. They have an encyclopedic knowledge of which cargo requires which handling protocol under which Charter provision and will cite chapter and clause when challenged.
~
