The Harbor Warden forward scout is making the maritime authority's territorial claim visible through the physical act of marking and documenting the boundary — each marker post placed, each notation made in the survey ledger, is intended to be used as evidence in the ongoing jurisdictional dispute between Mafdet's Harbor Charter and the Reach Warden commission's inland authority. They are specifically instructed not to initiate conflict with Reach Wardens encountered at the boundary, but to maintain the documentation that the Harbor Charter legal team is building toward a formal territorial settlement.
~
