a coastal fog phantom~
In the fog, a shape that is not quite a person and not quite a weather phenomenon moves with purposeful, hostile intent.
~
The coastal fog phantom is a seasonal apparition that manifests during the fog periods when the Tidemouth's characteristic marine layer rolls in from the sea and reduces visibility to arm's length. The entity appears to be constituted of the same fog — slightly denser, slightly colder, with a suggestion of features that shift when approached — and it is distinctly hostile to any presence in the fog zone during its active hours. Whether it is a weather spirit, a haunting, or something that exploits the fog as a medium for manifestation has been debated by the scholars at Measure's Rest without resolution. It is present only at night; the daylight disperses it with the fog.
~
