The assessment hall guardian was created by the Shoreward Compact's administrative architects to protect the physical conversion tables and the Seal from unauthorized access — it is a construct of the Threshold's specific institutional design, reflecting the Compact's intersection of inland and maritime authority in its physical form. Bronze elements from the maritime side of the conversion system and basalt components from the inland assessment infrastructure are worked together in its construction. It responds to unauthorized presence by applying the full enforcement authority of both jurisdictions simultaneously, which produces an effect considerably more severe than either alone.
~
