The water-debt phantom is bound to the Discharge Basin — the area where the Water-Debt Discharge was supposed to formally close the inland water-debt ledger and convert it to maritime credit — because the settlement itself was never completed. The Compact's collapse prevented the closing ceremony, leaving the phantom in perpetual calculation of a debt obligation that cannot be fulfilled because the institutional framework that would fulfill it no longer exists. It processes the Basin as an active debt settlement site and any intruder as an unregistered participant in the settlement who owes the outstanding balance.
~
