A shade in legal robes occupies the Oath Court with the gravity of someone who understands the full weight of the oaths sworn here.
~
The risk assumption shade is the spiritual remnant of the Oath Court's adjudicating authority — a shade that persists in the Court because the oaths sworn here were never discharged or abrogated, and the shade cannot leave until they are. It processes intruders as parties who have entered the Oath Court without filing the appropriate risk assumption declaration, which in the Threshold's legal framework made every person who passed through this space a co-guarantor of the outstanding oath obligations. The shade is enforcing that guarantorship with the full authority of a legal system that has been gathering interest on unpaid obligations for generations.
~
