The dual-seal sentinel is the guardian construct most specific to the Shoreward Compact's dual-authority mandate — it was created to embody both jurisdictions simultaneously, requiring both inland and maritime authorization to satisfy its verification protocols. In the Compact's operational period, this was the mechanism that ensured the dual attestation requirement was enforced at the physical level rather than relying solely on documentation checks. With neither inland survey authority nor maritime seal authority currently present in valid form, the sentinel has defaulted to treating all parties as unauthorized and applies both enforcement responses simultaneously.
