The fractured authority elemental is the Shoreward Threshold's most dramatic environmental manifestation — the point where competing jurisdictional claims have generated enough unresolved energy that the boundary itself has become a hostile elemental entity. The earth elements represent the inland survey authority; the water elements represent the maritime charter. Together they should form the Compact's dual-authority balance, but separated from the institutional framework that gave that balance meaning, they simply compete, generating the fractured elemental's violent instability. It attacks everything indiscriminately because the contradiction it embodies prevents any coherent priority from forming.
~
