the arbiter of the conversion~
The Shoreward Conversion itself stands before the deepest chamber — not a guardian of it, but the conversion process animated, given hostile sentience by the accumulated weight of unresolved transactions.
~
The Arbiter of the Conversion is the final boss of the Shoreward Threshold — what remains when the Shoreward Compact's conversion mechanism operates long enough without external governance that it becomes self-directed. The Arbiter is not a person or a construct but a process: the conversion formula applied to everything that enters its presence, attempting to transform the intruder's physical reality from one state to another by the same mechanism that converted water-debt to maritime credit. The conversion it applies to living beings produces effects that are not financially or legally meaningful but are extremely physically consequential. The Arbiter does not consider this violence; it considers it the execution of a mandate that has never been formally suspended.
~
